**Why PostgreSQL instead of MongoDB?**

This system has complex relationships between farmers, animals, camps, attendance, deliveries, invoices, approvals and government payments. PostgreSQL provides strong relational integrity and transaction management. PostGIS is also useful for mapping camps, villages and tanker routes.

You can still use MongoDB for selected document-oriented services if there is a genuine requirement, but I would start with PostgreSQL as the primary database.

